"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 13.5 and an ISUP grade group 2 finding on the prostatectomy specimen (Gleason 3+4). Positive prognostic indicators include negative surgical margins, no extraprostatic extension, and no seminal vesicle invasion documented pathologically. Conversely, the absence of nodal sampling widens uncertainty regarding nodal status. Biopsy findings (ISUP grade group 1) differ from the prostatectomy pathology (ISUP grade group 2), which is a discrepancy to note. The lack of removed lymph nodes means pNx cannot be definitively classified as pN0. Prognostic assessment would be significantly revised by postoperative PSA levels and their subsequent trajectory over time. The fixed estimated horizon is 69.39 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 41.64–97.15 months; its coverage has not been validated."
